cary/supabase/.temp/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Large reference assets (not needed for build) — hi-res leaf/bark scan sources.
# The wired, downscaled packs live under public/textures/ (tracked); these are the
# full-res originals kept locally for re-baking higher-res atlases.
assets/botanical-reference-hires/
assets/leaf-packs-2026/
models/
public/models/
# Allow the victorian lamp model (needed at runtime)
!public/models/lamp-posts/
!public/models/lamp-posts/victorian-lamp.glb
public/photos/lafayette-square/

# Raw data cache (regenerable via scripts/)
scripts/raw/*
# stl_parcels.json moved to cartograph/data/lafayette-square/raw/ (scene-homed)
!scripts/raw/osm_street_lamps.json

# Archived/defunct scripts
_archive/
# ...but the doc Diaries are tracked (cooled active docs, not defunct scripts).
!arborist/_archive/
!arborist/_archive/**
# ⭐⭐ cartograph's Diary was NEVER added here — the known "_archive gitignore gotcha"
# (BACKLOG §doc-pristineness, open since 2026-06-30; hit again 2026-07-31). Its 44
# tracked files predate line 58, so the rule silently swallowed every archive written
# AFTER it: trim-on-subsume quietly became deletion-with-extra-steps, in the exact
# doc that doctrine names the sanctioned downstream home (BOZ.md §0 "additive/archiving,
# never destructive"; git is the archive of record). Worst case is a brief moved from
# the (also-ignored) _handoffs/ to here — it then existed in NO tracked location at all.
!cartograph/_archive/
!cartograph/_archive/**
# Landscape intake — the operator's uploaded 3D set-pieces (DEM meshes, GLBs).
# LOCAL-ONLY by design: the landscape is a STAGE intake the operator uploads
# per-Look, deliberately OUT of the pour path so it can never be auto-swept into
# a slab (a20619cc — a stray sangabriel.obj in data/<scene>/ once baked the San
# Gabriels into Altadena). Baking is gated on an explicit design.landscape.source.
# Untracked was always the intent; this makes it so instead of leaving 34MB
# sitting in `git status` waiting for someone's `git add -A`.
cartograph/_landscape-intake/

# ── cartograph/data/<scene>/ — ONE SCENE-GENERIC RULE (2026-09-13) ───────────
# This was ~120 lines of hand-written per-town allow-lists. Towns poured after
# the last person edited this file were never given one, so their ENTIRE input
# set was ignored: the kit presented seven scenes and three of them could not be
# re-poured from a clone. Nothing errored — the Layer 0 silent substitution, and
# it failed worst on the towns nobody looks at.
#
# ⛔ A POUR ADDS NO LINES TO THIS FILE. Git's `*` matches one path segment, so
#    every rule below already reads <scene>. If you are about to type a town's
#    name here, the rule is wrong — fix the rule.
#    GUARD: node checks/claims-a-pour-adds-no-gitignore-lines.mjs
#
# ⭐ RETIREMENT IS NOT A RULE HERE EITHER. A retired town declares itself, in
#    its own directory: cartograph/data/<scene>/RETIRED.md says who retired it
#    and why, beside a one-line cartograph/data/<scene>/.gitignore that stops
#    its files re-emerging. No town is named in this file, retired or live.
cartograph/data/*
!cartograph/data/*/

# Not scenes: the pre-per-scene-layout relics that predate data/<scene>/.
# (A scene is a directory carrying neighborhood_boundary.json; these carry none.)
cartograph/data/clean/
cartograph/data/raw/

# raw/ — an ALLOW-LIST, deliberately. raw/ is the bulk fetch drop: elevation and
# canopy rasters, msbf building tiles, the _cache/, the *_raw.json fetch dumps.
# Only the reproducible-fetch INPUTS are kept. (The KIT POLICY below is about
# clean/, which is the opposite case — do not generalise one to the other.)
cartograph/data/*/raw/*
!cartograph/data/*/raw/osm.json
!cartograph/data/*/raw/osm_street_lamps.json
!cartograph/data/*/raw/admin_boundaries.json
!cartograph/data/*/raw/survey.json
!cartograph/data/*/raw/elevation.json
!cartograph/data/*/raw/centerlines.json
!cartograph/data/*/raw/measurements.json
!cartograph/data/*/raw/stl_parcels.json

# KIT POLICY (2026-07-18) — carried forward verbatim, because this comment is
# the thing that keeps the rule from being re-broken. clean/ carries the SOURCE
# census + maps a kit must let flow freely (park_census, the real wells,
# species-map, tree-mix, marker strokes). Track them ALL by default — do NOT
# re-add a per-file allow-list (that's the trap that silently dropped
# park_census + tree-species-map). Ignore ONLY the heavy GENERATED geometry,
# which the pipeline reproduces from source and must never bloat the repo.
#
# ⚠️ The trap was still live when this rule was written: LS's clean/ allow-list
#    was dropping clean/marker_strokes.json — operator-authored, written by
#    serve.js, tracked on every other town. Track-by-default is what caught it.
cartograph/data/*/clean/map.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/skeleton.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/ribbons.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/terrain.bin
cartograph/data/*/clean/terrain.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/derived_trees.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/elevation.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/street-index.json

# Dead classify-era output. ⛔ This is a CLOSED list, not a skip list: nothing in
# the tree writes these any more (they survive only in LS, dated 2026-03-30 and
# 2026-04-17), so a freshly poured town cannot produce one. They are ignored
# rather than tracked because 2.6 MB of output with no producer and no consumer
# should not enter the repo. Delete them from disk and this group goes with them.
cartograph/data/*/clean/block.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/fragment.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/island.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/park.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/parking.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/unknown.json
cartograph/data/*/clean/map.svg
cartograph/data/*/clean/preview.html

# Local-only operator rollback state: the .prebak / .prefetch-* snapshots a
# failed commit rolls back through (INTAKE §0.5, /rollback-extent). Regenerable
# by definition — they are a snapshot OF the tracked inputs.
cartograph/data/*/.prefetch-*/
cartograph/data/*/*.prebak
cartograph/data/*/*.prebak-*

# Everything else under a scene is TRACKED by the rule above and needs no line:
# the authored/fetched roots (neighborhood_boundary, geography, neighborhood,
# building-overrides, tree-species-map, tree-mix), all of content/ and its
# *.overrides.json sidecars, and identity-registry.json — FROZEN building
# identity (centroid-key -> permanent msbfId), a curated artifact a re-fetch
# must preserve, NOT regenerable output (R18, EXTENT-DESIGN §4).
cartograph/node_modules/

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/

# ribbons.json snapshot backups created by the pipeline scripts.
# Useful locally for rollback; never wanted in source control.
src/data/ribbons.json.backup-*

# FOR-species20K LiDAR dataset (~51 GB, used as input to the Arborist
# tree-baking pipeline). Lives locally; never committed.
# Source: https://zenodo.org/records/13255198
botanica/

# Arborist operator state + caches. Curated picks live in arborist/state/;
# .laz → .ply preview conversion cache lives in arborist/_cache/. Both
# regenerable; never committed.
arborist/state/
# EXCEPT the hand-encoded species priors files — load-bearing artifacts
# per Project: Li'l Vera Cycle 1 rev. 2 (2026-05-20). Future species
# onboarding follows the same hand-encode → run → refine cycle.
!arborist/state/
!arborist/state/*/
arborist/state/*/*
!arborist/state/*/botanical-priors.json
arborist/_cache/
arborist/.venv/

# Arborist raw-GLB library. Authoring-only source pool the Arborist
# reads from; never read by runtime. The published artifact runtime
# consumes is the per-Look bake at public/baked/<look>/, written by
# arborist/bake-look.js. Library is multi-GB and regenerable; never
# commit it. See ARCHITECTURE.md §1 for the publish-loop rule.
public/trees/

# (Atlas QA visualisations — `bake-look.js:658` writes one per atlas so you can eyeball
# the packing; nothing loads them at runtime, verified 2026-07-21. Their rule was here
# and is now SUBSUMED by `public/baked/` below and re-stated in upload-baked-to-r2.mjs's
# EXCLUDE, which is what actually keeps them out of the published slab now.)

# Local handoff/brief dispatch archive — kept on disk, out of git (Jacob, 2026-07-21).
# ⛔ The directory contents stay local: dispatch briefs are working state, and CARY-BRIEF.md
# is program/legal material this repo is PUBLIC enough that it must not carry.
#
# ⭐ TWO EXCEPTIONS, TRACKED ON PURPOSE (2026-09-02, Jacob). These two are not dispatch
# state — they are the DESIGN OF RECORD for an arc that is on the board (`ROADMAP.md H1`)
# and cited from source (`src/lib/renderTiers.js`). While they were ignored, every pointer
# to them was dead from a clone, so a scoped, designed, partly-built arc read as abandoned
# to anyone but Jacob. Reviewed line-by-line before tracking: pure render architecture, no
# credentials, clients or terms.
# ⚠️ NOTE THE GLOB: `_handoffs/*`, NOT `_handoffs/`. Git does not descend into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so a negation under a `dir/` rule never fires. This is the shape that works.
_handoffs/*
!_handoffs/HANDOFF-mobile-profile.md
!_handoffs/HANDOFF-preview-measurement.md

# D2 gate working artifacts (agent Plumb, 2026-08-08). `.d2-before.json` is the
# captured corner baseline (~1.4 MB) and `.d2-mutants/` holds generated COPIES of
# tileGround.mjs (~245 KB each) that the self-test builds and replays. Both are
# derivatives the tool regenerates on demand — the checker itself is tracked, its
# scratchpad is not. Dot-prefixed by the agent for exactly this reason.
scratch/.d2-*.json
scratch/.d2-mutants/
# The instrumented COPIES of tileGround.js that `claims-band-reaches-lu.mjs`
# builds (it now owns the loader `.d2-mutants/` used to hold). Same reasoning.
scratch/.band-probe/
# A10-③ (the iA source-edge stamp, 2026-08-09). Same rule, same reasoning: the
# checkers are tracked, their scratchpads are not.
# ⛔ `scratch/.iastamp-artifact.json` is deliberately NOT listed. It is COMMITTED,
# and that is right: at 396 bytes it survives a fresh clone, which is exactly what
# `ROADMAP` A10 complains that `a10-post-rim` does not do ("the baseline is not in
# git… regenerate it BEFORE you touch the cure"). A rule here would also be dead —
# gitignore never applies to a tracked file.
# ⚠️ But `claims-ia-source-stamp.mjs` PRINTS "…, gitignored" for it, which is false
# twice over. Fix the message, not the tracking.
scratch/.stamp-probe/
scratch/.fold-probe/
scratch/.mint-flip-*.json
scratch/.leg-probe/
scratch/.prov-probe/
scratch/.rekey-probe/
scratch/.notch-probe/
scratch/.rev-probe/
scratch/.lab-probe/
scratch/.arc-probe/
scratch/.ramp-probe/
scratch/.naip-spike/
scratch/_snapshots/

# ⛔⛔ THE WHOLE BAKED TREE IS UNTRACKED AS OF 2026-09-01 — IT LIVES IN R2.
# 516 MiB / 1138 files, growing 100–400 MB per town poured, against a 1 GB GitHub
# Pages limit. It is served from https://assets.theward.online/baked/<look>/… and
# reached at runtime through `src/lib/bakedUrl.js` (VITE_ASSET_BASE).
#
# ⛔ SO GIT IS NO LONGER WHAT CARRIES A POUR TO A VISITOR — THE UPLOAD IS.
# `cartograph/serve.js`'s bake endpoint runs `scripts/upload-baked-to-r2.mjs` as its
# last step and FAILS the request if it fails. Verify a slab actually landed with
# `node scripts/verify-baked-in-r2.mjs` — after every pour, and before you ever
# delete a local copy.
#
# ⚠️ TWO EXCLUSION RULES THAT USED TO LIVE HERE NOW LIVE IN THE UPLOADER, because
# once this whole tree is ignored the per-file rules below stop discriminating
# anything — every one of them matches an already-ignored path. They are NOT
# retired; they moved, with their reasons, to EXCLUDE in upload-baked-to-r2.mjs:
#
#   · lod0 (`*-lod0.glb`) — 353.3 MB the runtime cannot request:
#     `InstancedTrees#lodForRole` returns ONLY lod1/lod1far; the camera-distance LOD
#     swap (GeoTierDriver) was retired under role-at-bake. Still PRODUCED by
#     bake-look and kept on the authoring machine — just never published.
#     ⚠️ The Meteorologist canary resolves lod0 and will 404 until pointed at lod1.
#   · atlas viz sheets (`trees-atlas-*-viz.png`) — operator diagnostics, not payload.
#
#   ⭐ AND THE KTX2 RULE INVERTED, WHICH IS WHY THIS COMMENT IS REWRITTEN RATHER THAN
#   DELETED. It used to read "KTX2 pages ARE COMMITTED — do not re-ignore them; an
#   ignored page is a 404 in the canopy, not a rebuild." That was TRUE while the
#   deploy was an `actions/checkout` — being untracked meant being absent. It is now
#   FALSE by mechanism, not by decision: the pages ship via R2, so tracking has
#   nothing to do with whether they reach the canopy. The decision it protected —
#   *the canopy must have its pages* — is unchanged and is now enforced by
#   verify-baked-in-r2.mjs. `node arborist/pack-impostor-ktx2.mjs --look=<id>`
#   still regenerates them, and the pour still runs it as its last step.
public/baked/

# ── SCRATCH IMAGERY IS NOT COMMITTED ANY MORE (Jacob, 2026-09-12) ────────────
# "We've been cautious about saving things but as we continue toward
# productification clean precision is preferable."
# ⭐ THE RULE THIS FILE ALREADY STATES, APPLIED TO PICTURES: the checkers are
# tracked, their scratchpads are not. A forensic image is the scratchpad of a
# probe whose CONCLUSION belongs in a doc or a commit message — 110 files and
# 27 MB had accumulated, all of it regenerable by scripts already in git.
# ⚠️ THE 533 IMAGES ALREADY TRACKED IN scratch/ ARE UNAFFECTED. gitignore never
# applies to a tracked file; this stops the pile growing rather than rewriting
# what it already contains.
# ⛔ TWO EXCEPTIONS ARE COMMITTED ON PURPOSE and are not imagery:
#   scratch/_fx-stations.json  — a FROZEN BASELINE a tracked checker reads, and
#     regenerating it needs a checkout of a commit that still has ①. Same
#     reasoning as `.iastamp-artifact.json` above: a baseline that does not
#     survive a fresh clone is the thing ROADMAP A10 complains about.
#   scratch/design-backup-*.json — AUTHORED STATE. 18 blockCustoms entries. The
#     override is the product; this is the one class of file in scratch/ that
#     cannot be regenerated by running anything.
scratch/*.png
scratch/*.jpg
scratch/*.jpeg
scratch/*.gif
scratch/*.svg
scratch/AB.html

# Local marker: when this machine last published the shared player to staging R2.
# Read by the Publish button (`needsRebuild`) to skip a full vite build when the
# source has not moved since. Per-machine state, never shared.
.player-published

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⛔⛔ PHOTOGRAPH LIBRARIES ARE NOT SOURCE, AND GIT IS NOT AN ARCHIVE.
# Ruled by Jacob, 2026-09-22: "the bulky libraries must be git ignored." Measured
# the same day — roughly 1 GB was tracked and none of it is read by any code:
#   photos-wikimedia/              884 MB  LS's full-res Wikimedia originals
#   cartograph/data/huron/photos/   68 MB  huron's fetched originals
#   public/photos/<lots>/           81 MB  LS's per-listing web copies
#   authoring/cloud-photos/         19 MB
#
# ⭐ EVERY PHOTO LIBRARY HAS TWO TIERS AND BOTH ARE IGNORED:
#   ARCHIVE  the bytes as fetched or shot — cartograph/data/<scene>/photos/,
#            photos-wikimedia/. Not re-derivable.
#   WEB      ≤1600px, generated by cartograph/fetch-photos.mjs. Re-derivable from
#            the archive, so it never belonged in git at all.
#
# ⛔⛔ IGNORING IS NOT BACKING UP, AND THE ARCHIVE TIER IS NOT RE-FETCHABLE.
# `source_url` is not a durable path back: huron alone produced three local domains
# that lapsed inside a year and were re-registered by squatters. An ignored archive
# lives on exactly one laptop. ▶ It belongs in R2 (`theward-assets`, already wired by
# scripts/upload-baked-to-r2.mjs), which is also where a client's own copy will live.
# ⚠️ Until that upload exists, these directories are UNBACKED. Said plainly here
# rather than discovered later.
#
# ⚠️ And this stops the growth, it does not undo it: .git is 4.7 GB and history
# already holds every one of these blobs.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
photos-wikimedia/
authoring/cloud-photos/
cartograph/data/*/photos/
# ⛔ `public/photos/*/` — the SUBDIRECTORIES, not the directory. Git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded, so `public/photos/` + a `!` negation silently
# does nothing: git never descends far enough to see the exception. Excluding the
# per-listing folders leaves files sitting directly in public/photos/ visible.
public/photos/*/

# ⛔⛔ AND THE ONE FILE UNDER public/photos/ THAT IS NOT A LIBRARY. `og-preview.jpg` is
# the 164 KB link-preview image captured from Preview, and `cartograph/serve.js`
# STAGES IT ON EVERY PUBLISH (`slabPathspecs`). Ignoring it broke the Publish to
# Staging button outright: `git add` refuses an ignored path and the endpoint
# reports "git add failed".
# ⭐ The file beside it already warned about this exact class — slabPathspecs' comment
# explains why `public/baked/<id>` is DELIBERATELY ABSENT from that list, because
# staging an ignored path makes a publish that ships nothing while reporting ok. I
# created the same hazard one directory over and only escaped the silent version of
# it because `git add` happens to exit non-zero here.
# ⛔ A blanket ignore on a directory that mixes a deployed artifact with a bulk
# library is the defect. ⚠️ And the first fix did not work: `public/photos/` +
# `!public/photos/og-preview.jpg` still reported the file ignored, because git does not
# descend into an excluded directory and so never reads the negation. The rule above
# excludes `public/photos/*/` instead.
